uxlfoundation/oneTBB @ 8976636cbd89 (master, 2026-09-23): an in-register
machine_pause for WebAssembly worker threads.

picovoxel, an unofficial community TypeScript/WebAssembly binding of LEAP 71's
PicoGK, applies the same code change to its vendored oneTBB as the first hunk
of patches/oneTBB/0001-wasm-substrate-edges.patch. That file does not apply to
master (its Clang.cmake hunk lost its context), so this file carries the same
code regenerated for master, with the comment reworded.

The defect. WebAssembly has no pause instruction, so machine_pause takes the
generic branch (include/oneapi/tbb/detail/_machine.h:93-101), which ignores
`delay` and calls yield(). Under emscripten that is sched_yield, a call out to
JavaScript on every pause, so atomic_backoff's exponential shape collapses to
one JavaScript call per iteration.

The fix: on worker threads, an empty volatile asm loop that honours `delay`
and stays in-register. The main runtime thread keeps yielding, because
_emscripten_yield() drains the proxied-call queue there, and proxied
pthread_create (how worker threads launch under emscripten) blocks until that
queue is drained.

Output values: none; this changes only how long a spinning thread waits.

Measured (picovoxel, emscripten 5.0.1, Apple M2 Pro, 2026-07-26): 65.8 -> 2.1
ns per machine_pause(16) call on a worker (n = 9 and 10). A contended
spin_mutex showed no measurable change.

Applies with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` at the root of a oneTBB master checkout.
Independent of the other two oneTBB proposals.
Not applied by picovoxel's build; see upstream/README.md.

--- a/include/oneapi/tbb/detail/_machine.h
+++ b/include/oneapi/tbb/detail/_machine.h
@@ -51,6 +51,10 @@
 #include <thread> // std::this_thread::yield()
 #endif
 
+#if __EMSCRIPTEN__
+#include <emscripten/threading.h> // emscripten_is_main_runtime_thread()
+#endif
+
 namespace tbb {
 namespace detail {
 inline namespace d0 {
@@ -95,6 +99,19 @@
     while (delay-- > 0) { _mm_pause(); }
 #elif __ARM_ARCH_7A__ || __aarch64__
     while (delay-- > 0) { __asm__ __volatile__("isb sy" ::: "memory"); }
+#elif __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    // WebAssembly has no pause instruction, and the Generic fallback below is
+    // costly here: yield() lands on emscripten's sched_yield, which calls out
+    // to JavaScript on every pause, and it ignores `delay`, so atomic_backoff's
+    // exponential shape collapses to one JavaScript call per iteration. An
+    // empty volatile asm is a compiler barrier that emits no instructions, so
+    // the loop stays in-register and honours `delay`.
+    //
+    // The main runtime thread keeps yielding: _emscripten_yield() drains the
+    // proxied-call queue there, and proxied pthread_create (how worker threads
+    // launch under emscripten) blocks until that queue is drained.
+    if (emscripten_is_main_runtime_thread()) { yield(); return; }
+    while (delay-- > 0) { __asm__ __volatile__("" ::: "memory"); }
 #else /* Generic */
     (void)delay; // suppress without including _template_helpers.h
     yield();
